title The word a reader chose
prompt Continue copal's own live claim -- fleet_claim_scan.sh calls a board readable while the form guard beside it calls the same board malformed.
think The claim was opened and pushed on the lap before this one, and that lap was cut mid-send. The board carried it live with two hours left, so this lap inherited it rather than opening a second -- the card's own ask from last lap.
think The cold endurance run was already in flight at this lap's own HEAD, launched at 20260917.154711 against 1973d69b6d, so I held still through it rather than launching a second. It closed tree_moved=no, guards_run=355, 332 green, 21 red, 2 gated, 0 unrun. Not one red is mine; fleet_claim_form is absent from the list, which is last lap's phantom repair holding.
think The repair is one summary line. fleet_claim_scan.sh printed the fixed word form=readable beside its counts whatever fleet_claim_form_scan.sh answered. It now reads form=$form_verdict off that scan's own verdict= output, prints form=unread when no verdict line comes back, and adds one detail naming why a confined reading is reported rather than refused. The refusal above it still reads corrupting alone, untouched.
think I measured the class rather than reasoning about it. Replaying the form scan over all 370 revisions of construction/fleet-claims.kyri: 5 carried corrupting findings, which the reader already refuses, and 14 carried confined findings at corrupting zero -- every one a revision where the word was false.
obs The 14 are two windows of one class, not fourteen accidents: a what sentence holding the literal word claim mid-sentence, cut there by a hand. claim nobody over five revisions on 20260916, claim against over nine spanning 83 minutes on 20260917. In both windows every ship that opened a lap read form=readable before it built.
obs The data was never missing. confined=6 stood printed beside the word through both windows. What was wrong is that a summary substituted its own word for an instrument's -- which is why this reads as an aether finding rather than a counting one.
obs The mutation matters more than the legs. Restoring the fixed word must red the two new legs, or they prove nothing; it does, and the pen says so by name.
rota lap 5394, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; advanced by hand past row 4, which thirteen laps read today. The threshold page asks a lap to listen for the silence where a claim used to be, and the fixed word readable was exactly that -- a sentence nobody could hear over a word they trusted. The Lindy seat's rule lands on the same repair: a checked claim stays audible, an asserted one fades.
